    "rationale": "Chosen yolov8 to satisfy the medium latency and reasonable accuracy requirements on a MacBook Air with Apple M4 and Metal acceleration. YoloV8 is designed for efficient inference and good performance across varied object scales, which helps detecting persons, dogs, and cats at different distances and under occlusion. The dataset mix (openimages, coco, LVIS, etc.) supports learning robust features for the three classes in both indoor and outdoor contexts, supporting the target mAP@0.5:0.95 around or above 0.40 and per-class recall of at least 0.75 when trained with appropriate data augmentation and balanced sampling. Latency is expected to be around the target 500 ms per image on target hardware with a typical batch size; actual measured latency should be validated on device. CPU only feasibility is not assumed; Metal acceleration is preferred. If Metal path constraints become prohibitive, a fallback option is SSD300_coco or faster-rcnn_r50_fpn_1x_coco can be used, though with potential reductions in speed or accuracy. Consider 8-bit quantization and minor pruning if memory or latency become restrictive. The stated latency category is Medium and the accuracy target is 0.4 mAP with per-class recall >= 0.75.",
